 situations. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le16ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The First Conditional "}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You can use the first conditional to talk about possible actions and situations in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are two parts to the sentence.<br/><br/>  One part is the <span class=\"strong\">condition</span>. The other part is the <span class=\"strong\">result</span>. <br/><br/>Form:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">If</span>* + <span class=\"italic\">subject</span> + <span class=\"italic\">Simple Present tense</span>  + <span class=\"italic\">subject</span> + <span class=\"italic\">will/won't</span><br/>You use a comma after the condition in this form.<br/><br/>  *You can use other words instead of <span class=\"italic\">if</span>, you can use <span class=\"italic\">before</span>, <span class=\"italic\">after</span> or <span class=\"italic\">when</span>. <br/><br/>  You can flip the two parts of the sentence so that the result comes first. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Condition\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Result\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Before you start, </span><br/><br/>  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">After your meeting,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">you may want to speak to the editor.</span><br/><br/>   <span class=\\\"italic\\\">we will chat.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Result\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Condition\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You'll need to give me a draft of your article</span><br/><br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">This will be your first assignment</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">when you come to see me.</span><br/><br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">if this is of interest to you.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "editor in chief"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the person who is in charge of a group of editors; editorial team "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I am your boss and editor in chief of this magazine."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le16ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about working at a magazine."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Asking for Clarification"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "If you don't understand what a person is saying, it is important to ask for clarification in a polite way.<br/><br/>Here are some expressions you can use to ask for clarification:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul> <li><span class=\"italic\">I'm not quite sure what you mean.</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic\">Sorry. I didn't get that (point) ?</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic\">What do you mean by...?</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic\">Did you say...?</span><l/i> <li><span class=\"italic\">Could you clarify that?</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic\">Could you give me an example?</span></li></ul>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Ms. Ryan, could you please clarify what it is I will write about? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Did you say a feature on the citizens? Sorry. I didn't get your point about the new editor. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Sorry. I didn't get your point about the new editor. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "copy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that is made to look exactly like another thing "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Here is a copy for you to keep."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le16ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "editorial calendar"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a listing of the planned items for upcoming issues of a magazine "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You will find this editorial calendar to be very helpful when you are planning your articles. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le16ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to focus on "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to give special attention to something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We will focus on the the citizens of Massachusetts."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le16ob07aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "feature"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a piece or pieces of writing about a subject in a magazine"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: We want to do a feature on important citizens. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le16ob07aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "public figure"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who is well-known to the public "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We want to focus on public figures. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le16ob07aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "notable "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "important; well-known "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are many notable public figures in America. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le16ob07aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "draft"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a piece of writing or a plan that is not finished  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You may bring me a draft of your article when you come in."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le16ob07aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "assignment"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a piece of work that is given to someone as part of their job "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This will be your first assignment with Cambridge Life"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le16ob07aud09"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to fit someone in"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to see someone, even when you have a lot of other things to do  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I hope he can fit me in to his busy schedule."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le16ob07aud10"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Think of important people in your city. Write their names down."}, {"type": "text", "content": "From your list, choose a person you would like to write about. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Do some research about them. What is their name? What was their job? Why are they important? What do or did they do? When were they born?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a paragraph using the information you found. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Proofread your paragraph. Read it to a friend."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "con